WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.898
Hedy Lamarr arrived in America in 1937 as a film star.

2
00:00:05.248 --> 00:00:09.186
She was born Hedwig Eva Maria Kiesler in Vienna on 9

3
00:00:09.186 --> 00:00:13.502
November 1914, the only child of a wealthy Jewish family.

4
00:00:13.852 --> 00:00:15.977
She became an actress as a teenager.

5
00:00:16.327 --> 00:00:20.615
Her first major role, in the Czechoslovak film Ecstasy,

6
00:00:20.615 --> 00:00:24.825
in 1933, made her famous and scandalous across Europe.

7
00:00:25.175 --> 00:00:27.447
That same year she married Fritz Mandl, a

8
00:00:27.447 --> 00:00:30.051
wealthy munitions manufacturer and arms dealer.

9
00:00:30.401 --> 00:00:33.815
In 1937 she left Mandl, and Austria.

10
00:00:34.165 --> 00:00:37.494
She reached America by way of London, where she met the Hollywood

11
00:00:37.494 --> 00:00:40.771
studio boss Louis B. Mayer, who was looking for European talent.

12
00:00:41.121 --> 00:00:43.784
Mayer gave her a new name, Hedy Lamarr, after

13
00:00:43.784 --> 00:00:46.566
his favorite silent-film star, Barbara La Marr.

14
00:00:46.916 --> 00:00:50.736
A few months after she left, Nazi Germany annexed Austria.

15
00:00:51.086 --> 00:00:53.470
Lamarr and her friend George Antheil, an

16
00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:56.867
avant-garde composer, were fierce opponents of the Nazis.

17
00:00:57.217 --> 00:01:00.039
The trick was to keep changing the radio frequency.

18
00:01:00.388 --> 00:01:03.385
A transmitter on a ship and a receiver in the torpedo

19
00:01:03.385 --> 00:01:06.609
would hop from frequency to frequency at the same moment,

20
00:01:06.609 --> 00:01:10.002
guided by matching paper rolls like those in a player piano.

21
00:01:10.352 --> 00:01:13.707
They filed the patent on 10 June 1941.

22
00:01:14.057 --> 00:01:15.334
Their patent explains:

23
00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:20.973
“In a conventional player piano record there may be 88 rows of perforations.”

24
00:01:21.573 --> 00:01:25.668
It was granted on 11 August 1942 as U.S.

25
00:01:25.668 --> 00:01:30.582
Patent 2,292,387, "Secret Communication System."

26
00:01:30.932 --> 00:01:35.822
Hedy Lamarr became a United States citizen on 10 April 1953, sixteen

27
00:01:35.822 --> 00:01:40.928
years after she arrived, at a ceremony in federal court in Los Angeles.

28
00:01:41.278 --> 00:01:45.783
In 2014 they were inducted into the National Inventors Hall of Fame.

29
00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:49.593
What would you invent if you could work on any problem, with any partner?
